{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"25a69babd0dfa523311b6214d9ac1dc147efd1f5436e82290dfb6ee0ef76d5c6","digest":{"component_or_area":"gate-snapshot janitor","key_entities":["rebar._snapshot.janitor","rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger","JanitorConfig","max_entries","REBAR_GATE_MAX_ENTRIES","REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR","rebar-gate-snapshots","run_gc","DEFAULT_MAX_ENTRIES","tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py"],"problem_keywords":["gate-snapshot accumulation","filesystem metadata pressure","fseventsd resource exhaustion","unbounded entry count","snapshot retention"],"propositions":["The janitor's reclamation axes (free_watermark_bytes, max_bytes, max_age_seconds) remain inert on large mostly-empty volumes because they measure only disk pressure and age, not entry count.","13,000+ snapshot entries under REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR drove fseventsd to 26.3 GB RSS and >150% CPU on a 1.8 TiB volume with 886 GiB free space, exhausting swap and pushing load to 58 on a 6-core host.","A new max_entries axis with default 2000 (ON by default) must engage independently of disk headroom to bound filesystem metadata pressure.","The count-denominated reclamation must compose with existing hysteresis (target = max_entries * 95 // 100) and grace_seconds protection via the wants_room join in _reclaim_loop."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787898907358019509,"uuid":"192796b0-7158-4a8e-9486-fe6d611e36ce"}